/*QUAKED worldspawn (0.5 0.5 0.5) ?
Editor container for level brushes. Not an NSD entity type.
This profile saves source .map files; NOD binary export is not implemented.
*/

/*QUAKED ghost (0.2 0.8 1.0) (-16 -16 -24) (16 16 40)
Player entity type observed in StarCraft Ghost NSD scene data.
The displayed bounds are an authoring aid, not verified engine collision bounds.

"origin" - Source position in editor Z-up coordinates.
"angles" - Source pitch, yaw and roll in degrees.

These source keys are an authoring convention. Conversion to NOD's left-handed
coordinates and NSD property tags must be implemented and tested by the compiler.
Placing this entity does not yet produce a playable spawn.
*/

/*QUAKED misc_model (0.6 0.8 0.4) (-8 -8 -8) (8 8 8)
Editor-only static decoration prop. This is not an NSD entity type.

In NODscene preview maps, nsd:<offset> aliases represent verified native entities;
only origin, angles, and existing nod_sector may be edited.
The nil:world alias (nod_role nil_geometry) previews static NIL geometry:
ALL its fields, including origin and angles, are read-only. Do not add/delete.
Version-5 aliases use direct NOD/NMB references and immutable _frame values.
Only NIL static geometry retains an OBJ preview; all materials use textures/nod.
The bridge preserves native units (scale 1). Do not add scale or remap keys to
bridge aliases; those keys remain available for ordinary authoring props.

"model" - VFS-relative NOD or NMB path, e.g. 3D/Models/example.nod.
"_frame" - Zero-based NMB model-entry index. NOD uses 0.
"origin" - Source position in editor Z-up coordinates.
"angles" - Source pitch, yaw and roll in degrees.
"modelscale" - Uniform scale (default 1).
"modelscale_vec" - Per-axis scale, overriding modelscale.
"_remap0" - Optional native material remap: textures/nod/old;textures/nod/new.

Models use source coordinates, native UVs and LOD 0. Skinned meshes are shown
in rest pose; animation playback is not implemented. The original asset tree
is read-only. Map saving preserves references, not copies of model geometry.
NODscene patches supported bridge edits back into archived NIL/NSD/NPD copies;
new binary geometry and arbitrary new entity compilation are not implemented.
*/

/*QUAKED nod_scene (0.6 0.6 0.6) (-4 -4 -4) (4 4 4)
Immutable NODscene source binding; do not edit, add, or delete.
"nod_id" - Stable identity.
"nod_schema" - Source/preview schema, including native-model version 5.
"nod_sources" - Native source checksums.
*/

/*QUAKED nod_nil_sector (0.2 0.7 1) (-8 -8 -8) (8 8 8)
Read-only sector center, flags, and portal count; not a decoded sector volume.
*/

/*QUAKED nod_nsd_entity (1 0.6 0.2) (-8 -8 -8) (8 8 8)
Native scene point. Only origin, nod_rotation, and existing nod_sector are
editable. Identity, type, region, asset, frame, and status are read-only.
Trigger bounds/scripts remain opaque in the sidecar. The 16-unit selection
marker is not a native bound and is not rotated by nod_rotation.
*/

/*QUAKED nod_npd_waypoint (0.2 1 0.4) (-4 -4 -4) (4 4 4)
Native navigation-space waypoint; alignment with world space is unverified.
Only origin, nod_flags, nod_color, and nod_extra are editable.
The 8-unit box is a selection marker, not a native bound. Do not add/delete.
*/

/*QUAKED nod_npd_link (0.4 0.7 0.4) (-2 -2 -2) (2 2 2)
Native adjacency metadata, not a rendered graph edge.
Only nod_from, nod_to, nod_cost are editable; endpoints are record indices.
Do not add/delete links.
*/
